<title>BANGLADESH: Chittagong port handles 17,278 tonnes of cargo.</title>
<headline>Chittagong port handles 17,278 tonnes of cargo.</headline>
<dateline>CHITTAGONG, Bangladesh 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bangladesh's main Chittagong port handled 17,278 tonnes of export and import cargo in 24 hours ending 1.0 p.m. (0700 GMT) on Tuesday compared with 18,708 tonnes in the same period on Monday, port officials said.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>					 Monday		  Previous</p>
<p>    Export cargo		   4,331		   3,736</p>
<p>    Import cargo		  12,947		  14,972</p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at Chittagong port:</p>
<p>    Commodity	   Tonnes	 Ship</p>
<p>    Berthing Wheat    25,000     Akadan Bulk	2/10</p>
<p>    Sugar		 13,000     Mare		 3/10</p>
<p>    Cement		20,000     Golden sunlight  4/10</p>
<p>    Peas		  22,925     Nand Sristi	5/10</p>
<p>    Fertilizer	  26,559     INCE-B	    11/10</p>
<p>-- Dhaka Newsroom 880-2-506363</p>
</text>
